<h2>Move Around Fast</h2>

<p>
    Quickfire provides several ways to navigate quickly:
</p>

<h3>Global Search</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Press "/"</strong> – Instantly jump to the search box from anywhere in Quickfire</li>
    <li><strong>Use arrow keys</strong> – Navigate through search results without using the mouse</li>
    <li><strong>Press Enter</strong> – Open the selected result</li>
    <li><strong>Press Ctrl+Enter</strong> – Open the selected result in a new tab</li>
    <li><strong>Type to filter</strong> – Start typing to filter results as you search</li>
</ul>

<p>
    The search box finds clients, policies, renewals, and more—making it the fastest way to jump to what you need.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the search box with a cursor already focused and search results showing. Show the keyboard shortcuts as tooltips or annotations. Include examples of search results. -->

<h3>Help Panel Navigation</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Use the folder breadcrumb</strong> – Click the breadcrumb at the top of the help list to back up without scrolling</li>
    <li><strong>Quick navigation</strong> – Jump between help sections quickly using the navigation</li>
    <li><strong>Search within help</strong> – Use Ctrl+Shift+F to search within long help pages</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the help panel showing the breadcrumb navigation and folder structure. Highlight the breadcrumb and show how it works. -->

<h2>Voice and Triggers</h2>

<p>
    Quickfire supports voice commands and smart triggers for faster interaction:
</p>

<h3>Voice Commands</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Hold the glowing Q icon</strong> – Press and hold the Q icon to speak a command when typing is slow</li>
    <li><strong>Speak naturally</strong> – Use natural language like "Show me Acme Manufacturing's policies"</li>
    <li><strong>Release to process</strong> – Let go of the Q icon to process your voice command</li>
    <li><strong>Use when convenient</strong> – Great for hands-free operation or when typing is difficult</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Voice commands work with Enhanced AI Chat, so you can use them for any chat interaction.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Graphic of the Q icon with a short caption like "Hold to talk". Show the icon in context with a visual indicator that it's being held. Include a brief animation or visual cue. -->

<h3>Trigger Links</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Click to open</strong> – Regular click opens the trigger link</li>
    <li><strong>Ctrl+Click</strong> – Copies the trigger link to your clipboard</li>
    <li><strong>Ctrl+Shift+Click</strong> – Runs the Outlook search tied to the trigger</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Trigger links appear throughout Quickfire and provide quick access to related information or actions.
</p>

