<h2>Stay Oriented</h2>

<p>
    Keep your workspace organized and easy to navigate:
</p>

<h3>Help Panel Management</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Pin the help panel</strong> – When learning a new workflow, pin the help panel so it stays visible</li>
    <li><strong>Collapse when confident</strong> – Once you're comfortable, collapse it to save screen space</li>
    <li><strong>Toggle as needed</strong> – Show or hide the help panel depending on what you're doing</li>
</ul>

<p>
    The help panel is your guide—use it when learning, hide it when you're in the flow.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Side-by-side showing the help panel pinned (visible) and collapsed (hidden). Show the pin/unpin button and how the interface changes. -->

<h3>Search Within Pages</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Use Ctrl+Shift+F</strong> – Search within long help pages or any text content</li>
    <li><strong>Find quickly</strong> – Jump to specific sections without scrolling</li>
    <li><strong>Works everywhere</strong> – Use this shortcut in help pages, forms, and other text areas</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot showing the find/search dialog (Ctrl+Shift+F) in action on a help page. Show search results highlighted. -->

<h2>Keep Things Tidy</h2>

<p>
    Maintain a clean, organized workspace:
</p>

<h3>Help Panel Refresh</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Refresh after adding pages</strong> – Refresh the help panel after you add a new help page so it appears right away</li>
    <li><strong>Stay current</strong> – Keep the help list up to date with the latest content</li>
</ul>

<h3>Naming Conventions</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Use short names</strong> – Use short, clear names for your own help pages so they're easy to spot in the list</li>
    <li><strong>Be descriptive</strong> – Names should clearly indicate what the page covers</li>
    <li><strong>Organize logically</strong> – Group related help pages in folders</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of a help page list showing clear, short names that are easy to scan. Show examples of good naming vs. overly long names. -->

<h2>Keyboard Shortcuts</h2>

<p>
    Master these keyboard shortcuts for faster work:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>/</strong> – Jump to search</li>
    <li><strong>Ctrl+Shift+F</strong> – Find in page</li>
    <li><strong>Ctrl+Enter</strong> – Open search result in new tab</li>
    <li><strong>Ctrl+Click</strong> – Copy trigger link</li>
    <li><strong>Ctrl+Shift+Click</strong> – Run Outlook search from trigger</li>
</ul>

<p>
    These shortcuts work consistently throughout Quickfire, making navigation faster once you learn them.
</p>

